# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in ONE of the options below.
# .env.local is gitignored — never commit a real key.
#
# Until one is set, the contact form still works: it detects that email is not
# configured and offers the visitor a prefilled mailto link instead, so a
# message is never accepted and then silently dropped.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 1 — Web3Forms (recommended for now: no domain needed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Go to https://web3forms.com
# 2. Enter the home's email (pgsamuel07@gmail.com) and press Create Access Key
# 3. The key arrives in that inbox — paste it below
# 4. Enquiries then arrive at that Gmail address, with reply-to set to the
#    sender, so hitting Reply goes straight back to them
#
# Free tier covers 250 submissions/month, which is far above what this site
# will see. No domain, no DNS records, nothing to renew.

WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 2 — Resend (better once the home owns a domain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resend will not send to arbitrary recipients until you have verified a domain
# in its dashboard, so this cannot be used before the domain exists. Once it
# does, this is the better choice: mail comes from the home's own address
# rather than a relay, which is less likely to land in spam.
#
# ENQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL must be at the verified domain, e.g.
# website@shalomchildrenshome.org

RESEND_API_KEY=
ENQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=
